We come back from the park.
We enter the flat.
I look at the clock on the wall.
It is almost eight o'clock.
I remember Asha's rule.
Moti must eat breakfast at exactly eight o'clock.
I go into the kitchen.
I open the heavy bag of dog food.
Moti understands immediately.
He jumps up excitedly.
I pour food into his steel bowl.
Moti barks loudly and comes to me.
I speak to him firmly.
"Moti, wait!" I say.
"Do not jump right now."
He listens to me and sits down.
I check the clock again.
Now it is exactly eight o'clock.
I place the bowl on the floor.
"Good boy."
"Now eat it," I tell him.
Moti happily eats his breakfast.
